id: CSS-AP-012
ilities: [modifiability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: Code quality antipatterns
category: antipattern
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .css .scss .less
  exclude_paths: node_modules/ vendor/ dist/ build/
patterns:
  - regex: -(webkit|moz|ms|o)-[a-zA-Z-]+\s*:
    message: Vendor prefix may be redundant — use autoprefixer instead of manual prefixes
  - regex: @extend\s
    message: "@extend in SCSS creates implicit coupling and selector explosion — use mixins or composition"
  - regex: transition\s*:\s*all
    message: transition: all animates every property change — specify exact properties for performance
  - regex: calc\([^)]*[+\-][^ )][^)]*\)
    message: calc() operators need spaces (e.g., calc(100% - 20px)) — missing spaces cause silent failures
  - regex: ^(\s{16,})\S
    message: Deep nesting (4+ levels) — increases specificity and reduces readability
  - regex: opacity\s*:\s*0\s*;
    message: opacity: 0 hides visually but element remains interactive — add pointer-events: none if intended
  - regex: :\s*[0-9]{3,}px
    message: Large magic-number pixel values are hard to maintain — use variables or a spacing scale
  - regex: [a-zA-Z.#\[][^\{]*\s[a-zA-Z.#\[][^\{]*\s[a-zA-Z.#\[][^\{]*\s[a-zA-Z.#\[][^\{]*\s[a-zA-Z.#\[][^\{]*\{
    message: Selector with 5+ parts is overly specific and fragile — simplify to 3 or fewer
fix: Use autoprefixer for vendor prefixes, specify transition properties, and flatten deep nesting
